<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 23,973 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 23,973 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 23,973 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Friday compared to 31,124 tonnes in the same period on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Friday	August 13</p>
<p>    Export cargo		10,892	 8,184</p>
<p>    Import cargo		13,081	22,940</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, one ship sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, two are expected to sail and eight are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Vegetable oil	18,600	 Kristal		   Due</p>
<p>Fuel oil	     20,000	 Iliad		     Due</p>
<p>High speed diesel  70,000	 Chesapeak City	  17/8</p>
<p>-- Karachi Newsroom (9221) 5685192; Fax (9221) 5673428</p>
</text>
